## D4 finding → follow-up filed
The brief's premise "`wild --version` emits a version string" is false: wild handles no `--version` at all — it exits 2 and prints the JSON refusal envelope. ddl's generic probe degrades gracefully to `v?` (no crash, no garbage). No per-tool special-casing mechanism exists for non-npm tools, and D5 forbids installer changes, so nothing was added on the ddl side. Filed **wild-9sm** in the wild repo: "wild: implement `--version` so fleet version probes work" (P2) — a one-line wild-side fix that completes the probe story without this slice growing scope.

`versions.ddl.toml` untouched; compat semantics, installer, and the wild repo are all untouched as ordered.
